# Commit Completed Work

- After implementing and verifying a requested code change, create a git commit.
- Commit only files relevant to the completed task; preserve unrelated user changes.
- Use a concise German commit message describing the reason for the change.
- Do not push unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not commit when the task only inspects, explains, diagnoses, reviews, or plans.
